  "description": "Neighborhood retail strip with two drive-thru pads on 8.11 acres. EXAMPLE. Frontage on a 4-lane state highway (~30,000 vehicles a day) with growing rooftops behind it and no competing strip within a mile makes retail the most productive use. The test fit ranked pads on the frontage with a strip behind first by residual land value; storage and multifamily came out below it, office negative. Three drive-thru pads take the frontage (the market supports about 12,000 sf), the strip fills the depth, and one side pond holds the detention."
